CCIFA Sovereign License v1.0
==================================

Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Code & Craft International Federation Association (CCIFA).
All rights reserved, worldwide, in all 11 certified languages.

1. DEFINITIONS

   1.1 "CCIFA" means the Code & Craft International Federation Association,
        the international federation governing the Coding World Cup.

   1.2 "MatchCore" means the sovereign engine, source code, rule packs,
        dashboards, legal corpus, documentation and infrastructure made
        available under this License.

   1.3 "Sovereign Seal" means the cryptographic record produced by the
        SealEngine, comprising a chained SHA-256 root hash and an Ed25519
        arbiter signature.

   1.4 "Sovereign Ledger" means the append-only, SHA-256-chained JSONL
        ledger maintained by MatchCore.

   1.5 "Certified Languages" means the 11 official languages of CCIFA:
        EN, FR, ES, IT, DE, HI, PT, JA, ZH, KO, AR.

2. GRANT OF RIGHTS

   2.1 Subject to the conditions set out below, CCIFA grants you a
        worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free licence
        to:
        (a) use, study, and modify MatchCore for internal,
            non-commercial, sport-coding governance purposes;
        (b) reproduce and distribute verbatim copies of this License and
            the copyright notice with any verbatim copy of MatchCore.

3. CONDITIONS

   3.1 You may NOT represent a match, ranking, draft, transfer or seal
        as "CCIFA-certified" or "sovereign" unless it was produced by an
        unmodified MatchCore engine operating inside a CCIFA-accredited
        sovereign arena and signed by a CCIFA-licensed arbiter.

   3.2 You may NOT remove, alter or obscure any Sovereign Seal,
        chain hash, arbiter signature or ledger reference.

   3.3 You may NOT connect a sovereign arena node to any public network
        during an official match. Offline operation is mandatory.

